   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the radius of convergence of the power series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{4^{n}(x-5)^{2n+1}}{9^{n}} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         3,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For the ratio test, \\( \\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| = \\frac{4 \\left|{x - 5}\\right|^{2}}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               4,
               [
                  "Power",
                  [
                     "Abs",
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "x",
                        -5
                     ]
                  ],
                  2
               ]
            ],
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As \\( n \\to \\infty \\), the limit of this ratio is \\( \\frac{4 \\left|{x - 5}\\right|^{2}}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               4,
               [
                  "Power",
                  [
                     "Abs",
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "x",
                        -5
                     ]
                  ],
                  2
               ]
            ],
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series converges when \\( \\frac{4 \\left|{x - 5}\\right|^{2}}{9} < 1 \\), that is, when \\( \\left|x - 5\\right| < \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The radius of convergence is \\( R = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            2
         ]
      }
